From a4f0136b3d34d3965e6491205c13c35f351e32e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:55:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 347/638] printing: provide noninteractive AROS fallbacks

CEF requires basic printing symbols even before AROS has a native print-manager UI. Reuse Chromium's no-system-dialog PrintingContext and provide an explicit warning-only printer-manager action instead of importing Linux desktop process launchers.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: exact-link-gap-fixed-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: registered native link contained only PrintingContext::CreateImpl and PrinterManagerDialog::ShowPrinterManagerDialog from this boundary

AI_ASSUMPTION: capability absence is preferable to pretending a system dialog exists; future airprint.device integration replaces the UI fallback

AI_LIMITATIONS: printing behavior, compile, and native CEF link remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-zero-v8-native-link-20260725/04-undefined-symbols.txt

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
